  "findings": [
    "#25: activation waiting is not the dominant cost. Every one of the 16 c=1 rows records exactly one no_provider event, 16 events against 655 speculative cycles, or 2.44% of cycles. Eliminating it entirely bounds the gain at 2.44%, so the task's own stop condition applies and no priming change is warranted. first_fallback_position is null on every row, so the event is the activation cycle at the start, not a mid-generation loss.",
    "#32: budgets 4-6 cannot be swept on this artifact. A server pinned to --speculative-candidate-budget 5 reports resolved 5 at /v1/hipengine/capabilities and refuses both requests at admission with route_decision_reason=candidate_budget_not_qualified, effective_route=default, and zero MTP tokens. The deepest retained evidence row for this artifact is K=3, and the gate is a comparison rather than a clamp, so the sweep needs a new evidence row for a deeper cell (production numerical, quality, and performance artifacts) before any K=4-6 number can exist.",
    "#32, the trend below the bound: accepted drafts per cycle is still rising at K=3 (0.874, 1.608, 2.085/2.099) while each added verify row costs a rising amount of the dominant target window (+7.26 then +8.57 ms). Per-request decode still improved 19.81 -> 25.87 -> 28.01 tok/s, so saturation is not demonstrated at the deepest qualified budget; it is bounded by the evidence gate, not measured."
  ]
